      "body": "## Motivation\n\n`KTEPWrapperMethod.create_weights()` does not pass the layer's `swiglu_limit`\nto `KTMoEWrapper`. The native wrapper therefore defaults to `0.0` (disabled),\neven when the GPU runner and checkpoint require clamping. This omission is\nstill present on main at `3831e7e0918052be50ef38b3ff62154573e213d7`.\n\nWe found this while qualifying DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash with MXFP4 CPU expert offload\non dual EPYC 7443 (AVX2) and two RTX PRO 4500 Blackwell GPUs. The checkpoint's\n`text_config.swiglu_limit` is 10.0; resident GPU experts use it, but the CPU\nconfiguration silently received zero.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- Pass `layer.moe_runner_config.swiglu_limit or 0.0` to the native wrapper.\n- Register five CPU-only unit tests covering limits 10 and 7, `None`, zero,\n  and the non-owning TP rank. They exercise `create_weights` while replacing\n  only the native constructor/GPU weight-creation boundaries; no checkpoint,\n  GPU execution or installed `kt_kernel` is needed.\n- Keep native backend validation in charge of rejecting unsupported nonzero\n  clamp/method combinations instead of silently disabling model arithmetic.\n\nThis does not attempt to add support for other parameterized activations\n(`swiglu_alpha`, `gemm1_alpha`, etc.).\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\n- Executed the exact patched current-main `create_weights` function with the\n  five new tests in our deployed image's dependency environment: **5/5 pass**.\n  The standalone harness installed that function only in its own Python process;\n  it did not alter the server or installed source files. This is not a full\n  current-main dependency-stack or end-to-end run.\n- Negative control removing only the new keyword: the two nonzero-clamp cases\n  fail (`0.0 != 10.0`, `0.0 != 7.0`); the other three cases pass.\n- Independent native AVX2 MXFP4 primitive, rerun on both NUMA pools:\n  four identical routed tokens, one expert, hidden/intermediate size 128,\n  group size 32, one active coordinate. Gate projection 96, up projection 24,\n  and unit down projection produce **2304** with native limit 0 and **100**\n  with native limit 10. This verifies that the existing native backend honors\n  the setting when the caller supplies it.\n- The equivalent fix was deployed on our pinned V4.1 integration\n  (SGLang `1aa0e962b206102b7c439a4a0c4981cfec6e87bc` plus the community tree\n  patch, KTransformers `95009ea6856c0799e517e93cb12be5e8494bc7ce`). Fresh tool\n  calls, tool-result round trips and six fresh/cached/growing retrieval checks\n  near 126K input tokens passed without diagnostic hooks.\n\nThe native primitive and the omitted configuration are the correctness evidence;\nsuccessful model requests do not prove this omission caused every earlier\nbehavioral failure. The integration also has a separate streamed-GPU clamp fix.\n\nLocal CI command in a configured SGLang development environment:\n\n```sh\npython test/registered/unit/layers/moe/test_kt_ep_wrapper.py\n```\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nOn that pinned integration, three fixed-256-output runs after the fix had median\ndecode throughput **23.16 tok/s**, essentially unchanged from the preceding image.\nWarmed fresh prefill was about **365 input tok/s** end-to-end. These are deployment\nobservations, not a benchmark of pristine current main or an isolated attribution\nof every serving change to this one line.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- Formatting: isort 7.0.0 and ruff 0.15.1 checks pass for both changed files;\n  Python compilation and `git diff --check` pass.\n- CPU unit tests registered in `base-a-test-cpu`.\n- No serving API or user configuration changes.\n- Full current-main CI is left to upstream runners; model-quality, concurrency\n  and production acceptance are not claimed.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #38028533794](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38028533794)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #38028533596](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38028533596)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #38028533813](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38028533813)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
